WEBVTT

00:05:27.125 --> 00:05:30.893
There is no relationship
that doesn't have a power dimension.

00:05:30.917 --> 00:05:32.976
It's intrinsic to relationships.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.268
It's not good or bad.

00:05:34.292 --> 00:05:37.059
It's just part of the fabric
of relationships

00:05:37.083 --> 00:05:40.018
because in relationships,
people have expectations.

00:05:40.042 --> 00:05:41.893
And when you have expectations,

00:05:41.917 --> 00:05:46.226
it comes with a degree
of dependency, reliance,

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:49.101
and that dependency confers to the people

00:05:49.125 --> 00:05:52.518
on whom you depend power, by definition.

00:05:52.542 --> 00:05:55.143
And that power gets neutralized

00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:57.726
by making it become
something that is benevolent,

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.518
which we then call trust,

00:05:59.542 --> 00:06:03.268
so that it will become power to,
rather than power over.